          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.675,
            0.835,
            0.812
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The technique to draw the upper and the lower curves of the eye is the same as that used in the figure, ‘A Personʼ. Points A and B are the locations where the tip of the compass is placed when drawing the curves of the eye. Note that the upper curve and the lower curve should together form a symmetrical figure. For this to happen, where should these points A and B be placed? Make a good estimate."
            }
          ]
        },
